  "runner_up_case": "The claim is a present-tense custody assertion pinned to a hard as-of date, and the newest DIRECT evidence of incarceration is NY Mag's June 16, 2026 report from Lompoc — two weeks before the as-of date. Everything dated after 2026-07-01 is inferential, not primary: the July 13 'pardon still pending' item comes from a CryptoSlate prediction-market page summarizing DOJ pardon-attorney data (a stale or misread status is possible), and the July 16 Senate-resolution coverage only 'implies' continued incarceration. Clemency was live and contested in this exact window — Bankman-Fried had publicly petitioned Trump for a pardon, and the June 12, 2026 appellate affirmance had just exhausted his direct appeal, the classic trigger for a clemency grant or a Supreme Court cert petition with release on bail pending review. Any of those events in late June 2026 would make the claim FALSE while leaving nearly all the gathered evidence superficially intact. Critically, the team never captured a dated primary custody record: the BOP locator page fetched is just a search form, and the site:bop.gov snippets are undated, so no authoritative source on file affirmatively shows 'IN CUSTODY' for inmate 37244-510 on or after 2026-07-01. On the strict standard that a present-tense claim needs recent authoritative evidence, the record has a two-week gap at exactly the moment clemency risk peaked.",
  "would_flip_it": [
    "A BOP inmate-locator record for register number 37244-510 showing status RELEASED, home confinement, or residential reentry with a release date on or before 2026-07-01.",
    "A White House announcement or DOJ Office of the Pardon Attorney record showing a full pardon or commutation of Bankman-Fried's sentence granted before 2026-07-01 (which would also mean the July 13 'pending' status was stale or wrong).",
    "A court order — Supreme Court or Ninth Circuit — granting Bankman-Fried release on bail pending certiorari or further review, dated before 2026-07-01.",
    "Credible wire reporting (AP, Reuters, major outlet) that Bankman-Fried left BOP custody at any point in June 2026."
  ]
}
